// Tests for rcli::kde (bandwidths, density, ecdf, histograms) against R 4.3.3 (Rscript, %.17g).
//
// Measured agreement:
//   - bw.nrd0 / bw.nrd: last bits (checked at 1e-14).
//   - bw.ucv / bw.bcv / bw.SJ (ste, dpi), default nb = 1000 and R's coarse default tolerances: within 1e-13 relative
//     (checked at 1e-12), because the binning (1.01 * range / nb, trunc(x / d)), the search intervals (hmax), the
//     tolerances, the alternating 1.2x enlargement for "ste" and the zeroin iterates reproduce R's (all found by
//     black-box testing). With tol = 1e-10 the ucv/bcv minimisers agree to ~5e-8 (the criteria are flat at the
//     minimum and the sums are rounded differently; checked at 1e-7); SJ to 1e-13.
//   - density(): the grid ($x) and $bw agree to the last bit. $y is evaluated exactly (kernel sums) and agrees with
//     R's exact sum (computed in R as mean(dnorm(x0, x, bw)) etc.) to ~1e-15; R's own $y (linear binning + FFT)
//     differs from the exact values by up to 9.3e-4 * max(y) for the smooth kernels at n = 512 on these data
//     (relative error up to ~3e-2 where the density is small), and by up to 12% of max(y) for the discontinuous
//     rectangular kernel.
//   - ecdf, quantile(ecdf), nclass.*, hist breaks/counts/density, pretty(): exact (pretty() also matched R on 3000
//     random cases and hist() on 570 random data sets during development).
#include "rcli/kde.hpp"

#include <algorithm>
#include <string>

#include "check.hpp"

